.TH SH-VERIFY 1
.SH NAME
laplacianorder, laplacian7order \- shell script interface to verify(2)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B load verify

.B ${laplacianorder
.I n0 levels
.B }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Verify
is a loadable module for
.IR sh (1)
giving shell scripts direct access to
.IR verify (2)'s
convergence-order check for
.IR pde (2)'s
discrete Laplacian \(em the kind of study a shell loop is the natural
place to drive, not a compiled program.
.PP
.B ${laplacianorder}
runs the check at
.IR n0 ", 2" n0 ", 4" n0 ", ..."
resolution for
.I levels
levels, and yields one element per level: three space-separated
numbers,
.RI \(lq n " " error " " order \(rq,
the same fields
.IR verify (2)'s
own
.B Level
carries.  A caller typically loops over the result (after
.BR "load std" ,
for
.IR sh-std (1)'s
.BR for ):
.EX
	load std
	load verify
	for r in ${laplacianorder 8 5} {echo $r}
.EE
prints one line per level, the error shrinking and the observed order
climbing toward
.I 2.0
as resolution doubles.  A bad argument (fewer than 2 levels, or
.I n0
under 4) raises a
.B laplacianorder
exception with the same text
.IR verify (2)
would have returned.
.PP
.B ${laplacian7order
.I n0 levels
.B }
is the same for
.IR math (2)'s
three-dimensional
.BR lap7 ,
with
.I n
the interior width of a cube rather than the side of a square.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/sh/verify.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR verify (2),
.IR sh (1),
.IR sh-std (1),
.IR sh-pde (1)
